@page "/"

<PageTitle>Loom</PageTitle>

<section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">A programming language for Roblox</p>

    <h1>Write expressive Loom.<br />Compile to Luau.</h1>

    <p class="hero-description">
        Loom is a statically typed programming language that compiles to Luau.
        Explore the language, inspect the generated output, and experiment
        directly in your browser.
    </p>

    <div class="hero-actions">
        <NavLink class="button button-primary" href="playground">
            Open playground
        </NavLink>

        <a class="button button-secondary"
           href="https://github.com/rbx-loom/loom"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">
            View on GitHub
        </a>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="overview">
    <article>
        <h2>Typed</h2>
        <p>
            Catch mistakes before generated Luau reaches your Roblox project.
        </p>
    </article>

    <article>
        <h2>Familiar</h2>
        <p>
            Use readable syntax designed for structured Roblox development.
        </p>
    </article>

    <article>
        <h2>Open source</h2>
        <p>
            Browse the compiler, report issues, and contribute on GitHub.
        </p>
    </article>
</section>